==Battleground==
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A stage that could seem scary but with the right cats will be handle-able. At the start you should be able to stall the Oldhorn using any Relic CC units you have. Once you've saved up take out the Oldhorn, most preferably with a double bounty unit for extra money and send out any and all anti relic backliners to handle the M. Ost and Old horns. One such unit that you could use to take out M. Ost is Slapsticks Cats.

This stage is actually quite simple, as long as you bring [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|Anti-Relic]] crowd control units, some attackers, and some sturdy units. for example, you can bring a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]] (however limited by range), [[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Superstar Koneko]] (for her CC), and if you have them, [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]] work as attackers. As with the other stages in this Citadel, [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] can be used alongside each other to make short work of this stage.

